{"name":"Medium Lavender Magenta","hex":"#dda0fd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"medium","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The material of the surrounding environment, e.g. solid, liquid, gas, vacuum, or a specific substance such as a solvent.","The materials or empty space through which signals, waves, or forces pass."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of several common sizes to which an item may be manufactured, smaller than a large but larger than a small.","An item labelled or denoted as being that size."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medium"},{"term":"lavender","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of European plants, genus, Lavandula, of the mint family.","A pale bluish purple or violet colour, like that of the lavender flower."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Pertaining to LGBT people and rights."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lavender"},{"term":"magenta","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color which is close to the equal mixture of red and blue which is an additive secondary color but a subtractive primary color evoked by the combination of red and light blue."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the color of fuchsia, fuchsine, light purple."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magenta"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lavandula","blocks":[{"text":"Lavandula is a genus of 47 known species of perennial flowering plants in the sage family, Lamiaceae. It is native to regions of the Iberian Peninsula and Mediterranean coastline, the Middle East, extending to the Indian subcontinent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Single_lavender_flower02.jpg/330px-Single_lavender_flower02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavandula","wikidata":"Q171892"},{"title":"Magenta","blocks":[{"text":"Magenta is